Vitest custom matchers conventionally include `this: MatcherContext` (from `vitest`) as the first parameter so the implementation can access `this.isNot`, `this.utils.printReceived`, etc. Without it the `.not` path still works (because `pass` is honoured), but the signature is non-standard and will require a breaking change if the implementation ever needs matcher context utilities.

```ts
import type { MatcherContext } from 'vitest';
export function toHaveLiveRegion(
  this: MatcherContext,
  container: HTMLElement,
  options: LiveRegionMatcherOptions
): { pass: boolean; message: () => string }
```
